    "Notification history lives in a system database macOS protects, and Full Disk Access is the only permission that can read it. Backglance can’t request it — macOS has no prompt for this one — so the button above opens the setting.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {}
    },
    "Notification history lives in a system database that macOS protects. There is no narrower permission and no API for it — Full Disk Access is the only way any app can read it. This is also why Backglance is not in the Mac App Store.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {}
    },
